{"content":"h13.\n\n**Impl** — `markdown.service` (unexported struct, `internal/markdown/markdown.go:58`), a goldmark-backed implementation wrapping `goldmark.Markdown` (`md` field). It's the only concrete type in the codebase satisfying `markdown.Service`.\n\n**Construction** — built by `markdown.NewService(opts ...Option)` (`internal/markdown/markdown.go:85`), which configures goldmark with GFM plus optional tag/mention extensions. At runtime the one production call site is `v1.NewAPIV1Service` (`server/router/api/v1/v1.go:47-51`), which calls `markdown.NewService(markdown.WithTagExtension(), markdown.WithMentionExtension())` and stores the result on `APIV1Service.MarkdownService`. (Other call sites — `test_helper.go:44`, `rss_test.go:54`, `fileserver_test.go:427` — are test-only, each building a fresh instance for isolation.)\n\n**Holders of the interface** (`markdown.Service`-typed fields/params, all fed from that single `NewAPIV1Service`-built instance in production):\n- `v1.APIV1Service.MarkdownService` (`server/router/api/v1/v1.go:35`) — the origin holder; consumed directly, e.g. `memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload(ctx, ..., s.MarkdownService)` in `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108,447`.\n- `rss.RSSService.MarkdownService` (`server/router/rss/rss.go:45`) — populated via `NewRSSService(profile, store, markdownService)`; wired in production at `server/server.go:85` as `rss.NewRSSService(s.Profile, s.Store, apiV1Service.MarkdownService)`, i.e. the same instance created for the API service is reused for RSS rendering.\n- `memopayload.Runner.MarkdownService` (`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:16`) — the interface is a field on this runner and the ctor `NewRunner` takes it as a param, but `find_references`/`[ArchMap query]` show `memopayload.NewRunner` has no call sites anywhere in the repo — this holder appears to be dead wiring in production; the actual call path bypasses the `Runner` struct and calls the package function `memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload` (`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:74`) directly with `s.MarkdownService`.","iteration":24,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
